                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 7 at 3:12AM HST until September 8 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "Moisture along the eastern flank of Hurricane Lowell will bring\nperiods of heavy rain to the main Hawaiian Islands through Tuesday.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Kauai and Niihau.\n\n* WHEN...Through Tuesday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Significant flooding may occur due to the overflow of\nstreams and drainages. Roads in several areas may be closed, along\nwith property damage in urban or low lying spots due to runoff.\nLandslides may also occur in areas with steep terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Moisture along the eastern flank of Hurricane Lowell will bring\nperiods of heavy rain to the main Hawaiian islands through\nTuesday.",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
